<h2>A community assembling in real time</h2>
<p>
  In late 2017 a new species, the Puerto Rican crested anole (<em>Anolis
  cristatellus</em>), arrived on <a href="/research/lizard-island/">Lizard Island</a>,
  another semi-terrestrial specialist, and we have been watching its evolutionary
  battle with the resident brown anole population ever since. Our
  <em>Nature Communications</em> paper follows the two species from their first
  meeting through the divergence that followed.
</p>

<h2>Introductions with known start dates</h2>
<p>
  The tropical lizards that have arrived in Florida over the past century give us
  contemporary introductions with known start dates, allowing us to estimate both
  the adaptive pathways and the rate of evolutionary response.
</p>
